          "final_text_tail": "c/jinja2/loaders.py`:\n\n**Added:**\n- `PathTransform` type alias (`t.Optional[t.Callable[[str], str]]`) at module level (src/jinja2/loaders.py:24-27)\n- Optional `path_transform` parameter (default `None`, keyword-safe) to all six loaders: `FileSystemLoader`, `PackageLoader`, `DictLoader`, `FunctionLoader`, `PrefixLoader`, `ChoiceLoader`\n\n**Behavior:**\n- Each `get_source` saves the original name, applies the transform (if not `None`), then resolves with the transformed path \u2014 so `BaseLoader.load` (used by `env.get_template`) is covered automatically\n- `PrefixLoader.load` and `ChoiceLoader.load` (overridden methods) also apply the transform once at the top level before delegating to child loaders\n- `TemplateNotFound` is raised with the **original, untransformed** template name for clear error messages; the compiled template's `.name` also keeps the original\n- Transform exceptions propagate uncaught to the caller\n- `list_templates` and all existing behavior are unchanged when no transform is given\n\n**Verification:**\n- All 841 existing tests pass\n- A 15-case functional script confirmed: aliasing (fs/dict/function), path normalization, the PR's complex multi-rule transform (v2/ prefixes, mobile/, .tpl\u2192.html, empty string), composite-loader top-level transform applied exactly once, `TemplateNotFound` original-name semantics, exception propagation, explicit `None`, and full backward compatibility\n\nChanges are left in the working tree (uncommitted), and no existing tests were modified.",
